= Dagmar Ziegler

Dagmar Ziegler from the Prignitz in rural Brandenburg was a state minister there before she went to the Bundestag, where she was a spokesperson of the Seeheimer Kreis. She wants the party to stop ignoring the countryside.

- @agriculture
- @rural_campaign
- @depression
- @root: Return to main

@agriculture
title: Agricultural policy
subtitle: Use the agriculture ministry.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?][? if agriculture_minister_party != "SPD" or spd_in_government == 0 : The SPD does not hold the agriculture ministry. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and spd_in_government and agriculture_minister_party == "SPD"
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; agricultural_policy_timer -= 6; last_advisor_action = 1
go-to: agricultural_policy

@rural_campaign
title: Campaign in the countryside
subtitle: Show what we have done for rural areas.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?][? if rural_policy <= 0 : We have no rural policies to show yet. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer == 0 and rural_policy > 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); peoples_party_support += 1

We tour the small towns and villages with our record on farmland, buses and doctors.

@depression
title: Addressing the economic crisis
subtitle: Argue for the Zukunftsprogramm.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?][? if recession_seen == 0 : There is no economic crisis. ?][? if investment_adopted : The party has already adopted the plan. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and investment_adopted = 0 and recession_seen
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; investment_support += 2; center_dissent += 10; labor_strength += 1

We publish studies showing that public investment pays for itself over time. The idea is gaining ground in the party, though Netzwerk Berlin is unconvinced.

